    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, the only concrete test class) is green. \n\nDone. The change is implemented and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}` flow now returns a `selfLink` field equal to `/api/owners/` followed by the new owner's id.\n\nSince the `OwnerDto` is generated at build time from the OpenAPI spec and populated by a MapStruct mapper, I made two changes following the existing conventions for derived read-only fields (like `displayName`, `membershipNumber`, etc.):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` property (readOnly string) to the `Owner` schema, right after `id`, so it's generated onto `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(selfLink(owner))\")` and a `selfLink(owner)` default method that returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (null-safe when no id is assigned yet).\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest` (and the full suite) \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
